WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
Map data from its source to every processor, queue, cache, log, and backup.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.360
Label trust boundaries where information moves between user devices, local servers,

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:11.379
gateways, cloud accounts, providers, and third-party APIs.

00:00:11.379 --> 00:00:15.560
For each crossing, record the data class, purpose, recipient, encryption, retention,

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:16.844
and authorized identities.

00:00:16.844 --> 00:00:19.995
A diagram is valuable only when it reflects runtime behavior.

00:00:19.995 --> 00:00:23.170
Prompt filtering can block prohibited fields, detect secrets,

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:26.680
or redact identifiers before external use, but it is not infallible.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.847
Documents may reveal sensitive information through retrieved passages, filenames,

00:00:30.847 --> 00:00:32.840
embedded metadata, or summaries.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.075
Test filters against realistic inputs and define a safe action when classification is

00:00:37.075 --> 00:00:37.615
uncertain.

00:00:37.615 --> 00:00:40.030
Some data should never enter an automatic cloud route.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:42.750
Logs deserve the same classification as prompts and outputs.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:46.160
Gateways, model servers, tracing tools, application telemetry,

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:50.560
and provider consoles may record content, tokens, account identifiers, errors,

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:51.490
and tool calls.

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:55.480
Minimize content logging, restrict access, encrypt transport and storage,

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.115
and set retention intentionally.

00:00:57.115 --> 00:01:00.785
Confirm provider data-use and deletion terms rather than assuming an API request

00:01:00.785 --> 00:01:02.480
disappears after the response.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.930
Enforce policy close to the routing decision and again at destination access controls.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:11.130
Maintain evidence of which route processed a request without retaining unnecessary

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:11.710
content.

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:16.130
Review data flows when a model, provider, plugin, or observability tool changes.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:19.915
Hybrid privacy depends on controlling copies and metadata throughout the path,

00:01:19.915 --> 00:01:22.320
not merely keeping the original document local.
